From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: a dynamic buffer an embedder points at storage it imported

ID3D9VkInteropDevice1::BindBufferStorage renames a directly mapped D3D9
vertex or index buffer to a VkBuffer range the embedder imported, recorded
on the device as a discard renames it, so commands recorded before read the
old storage and those after the new. It is the D3D9 counterpart of
ID3D11VkExtContext2::BindBufferStorage and takes the same
DxvkBuffer::importStorage: accel-virt points a guest buffer the CPU writes
at the guest memory the guest writes it in. Buffers that are not directly
mapped keep a separate staging buffer and are refused. FlushCommands submits
what was recorded without waiting for the CS thread. MarkSubmission calls the
embedder back from a DXVK thread once the submission holding that point has
completed, which is how it follows a batch without polling an event query.
UnbindBufferStorage gives a buffer storage of its own again whatever the lock
flags and discard settings, BufferStorageBindable tells whether a buffer can
take imported storage, and WaitForIdle drains the CS thread, the submission
and finish threads and the device.
---
diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_common_buffer.h b/src/d3d9/d3d9_common_buffer.h
index aab28cb6..906b73c2 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_common_buffer.h
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_common_buffer.h
@@ -138,6 +138,11 @@ namespace dxvk {
       return m_allocation;
     }
 
+    inline Rc<DxvkResourceAllocation> ImportMapSlice(const DxvkBufferImportInfo& importInfo) {
+      m_allocation = GetMapBuffer()->importStorage(importInfo);
+      return m_allocation;
+    }
+
     inline Rc<DxvkResourceAllocation> GetMappedSlice() const {
       return m_allocation;
     }
